turnip/kgsl: do not fail the instance when VK_KHR_display is enabled

With the msm backend built as well (needed for the X11 WSI's DRM image
path), VK_KHR_display is advertised and clients such as vkcube enable it.
KGSL has no display, but the WSI already reports no displays without a
display fd, so there is no reason to refuse the device.

1857:   device->master_fd = -1;
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
@@ -1898,11 +1898,10 @@
 VkResult
 tu_knl_kgsl_load(struct tu_instance *instance, int fd)
 {
-   if (instance->vk.enabled_extensions.KHR_display) {
-      return vk_errorf(instance, VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED,
-                       "I can't KHR_display");
-   }
-
+   /* VK_KHR_display is advertised when the DRM backend is built too. KGSL
+    * has no display: the WSI gets no display fd (master_fd stays -1) and
+    * simply reports no displays, so the instance need not fail.
+    */
    struct tu_physical_device *device = static_cast<struct tu_physical_device *>(
       vk_zalloc(&instance->vk.alloc, sizeof(*device), 8,
                 VK_SYSTEM_ALLOCATION_SCOPE_INSTANCE));
